+# Cognitum C15 — Appearance Association R2
+
+Status: **experimental / research-only**; no Lu host integration, no authenticated identity, no independent detector.
+
+## Changes versus frozen real-image R1
+
+1. **Adaptive appearance weighting** — reduce image-match influence when competing track templates are visually indistinguishable. Model confidence is heuristic; not calibrated.
+2. **Guarded feature updates** — do not assimilate ambiguous matches into the active appearance representation; use conservative EMA for clear matches.
+3. **Additional real-image appearance evidence** — pinned 128-dimensional spatial HSV descriptor from actual image pixels alongside the existing pinned 128-D grayscale descriptor. These are handcrafted features, **not** learned ReID.
+4. **Improved motion** — 4D center/velocity Kalman filter with explicit process noise, innovation-covariance (Mahalanobis) gating and Joseph-form covariance correction. No camera-motion compensation or physical calibration is claimed.
+5. **Bounded long-gap gallery** — retain prior reliable templates for confirmed tracks and attempt appearance-constrained re-entry up to a configured finite age.
+6. **Ambiguity management** — evidence-journal alternatives, frozen unreliable updates, optional abstention with ephemeral tentative identities. Forced labels may be exported **only** to a benchmark and are never identity authorization.
+7. **Size/geometry consistency** — box-size-ratio gating and soft overlap cost.
+
+Every change is a switch in `R2Config`, so it can be individually disabled for ablation. All outputs are hypotheses. The R2 report contract lives at `proto/cognitum/spatial/v1/appearance_r2.proto`; the prior schema remains unchanged. Hashes bind feature bytes to image/frame/box, **not** sensor authenticity.
+
+## Experimental designs
+
+- `tools/run_c15_r2_real_images.py`: R2 strict ambiguity-abstention and no-color ablation vs frozen R1/MPNTrack on P2K's three selected MOT17 sequences.
+- `tools/run_c15_r2_forced_ablation.py`: offline-only forced top-1 alternative, explicitly unauthoritative, with ambiguity and blocked-update counts; trained settings are not learned or auto-tuned.
+- Original MPNTrack detections are unchanged and GT IDs never enter the associator. This remains identity-only and **not** an independent end-to-end tracking system.
+- `--DO_PREPROC True` is required for official TrackEval MOT17 scoring, with pinned TrackEval source and independently obtained MOT17 training labels.
+- **No broad generalization claims**: these three sequences have already been inspected and are not a fresh holdout. Re-evaluate against unseen sequences and independent detectors before accepting a performance improvement.
+
+## Minimal verification
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=. python -m pytest -q tests/test_c15_r2_appearance.py
+PYTHONPATH=. python tools/verify_protobuf_schemas.py --require
+```
+
+### Never interpret a forced benchmark ID as authority
+
+Even when an offline benchmark requires an ID in every MOT record, a near-tied match is still unverified. Lu is never modified or granted an action based on these assignments.
